macOS: describe the GICv2m frame of Hypervisor.framework's GIC

FreeBSD's vgic takes MSIs as writes to GICD_SETSPI_NSR and the device
tree says so with "mbi-ranges".  Hypervisor.framework's GIC has no
message-based SPIs in the distributor (GICD_TYPER.MBIS is clear, so
Linux ignores "mbi-ranges" and falls back to INTx); it has a GICv2m
frame instead.  Put that frame in the device tree, make it the PCI
bridge's MSI parent, and tell hvf/ where it is.

